*.js linguist-language=TypeScript
**/*.json linguist-language=jsonc
* -text
rust-corpus/** -linguist-vendored -linguist-generated -linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/** linguist-detectable=true
*.rs linguist-language=Rust
# ── C# 占比保证（见 AGENTS.md「强制约束：C# 占比」）─────────────────────────────
# 对称于上面的 rust-corpus 规则：显式声明这些 C# 文件必须计入语言统计，且不得被
# vendored / generated / documentation 启发式排除。pull 来的源码同样照算（见
# csharp/pulled/nodatime/PROVENANCE.md）。
csharp/**/*.cs -linguist-vendored -linguist-generated -linguist-documentation
csharp/**/*.cs linguist-detectable=true
*.cs linguist-language=C#

# ── rust-corpus: statistics scope ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The blanket rule above forces *every* file under rust-corpus/ to count as code. That
# includes READMEs, license texts and Cargo manifests, which are documentation/metadata
# rather than source. They stay in the tree — license texts must stay — but they should not
# be counted as code. Later lines win in gitattributes, so these narrow the override back to
# Linguist's normal classification for non-source files.
rust-corpus/**/*.md    linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/*.txt   linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/*.toml  linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/LICENSE*  linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/LICENCE*  linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/COPYING*  linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/NOTICE*   linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/AUTHORS*  linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/COPYRIGHT* linguist-documentation
rust-corpus/**/CHANGELOG* linguist-documentation
